  <prompt>Wire the FR-10 documentation set together: (1) add a "Component Layer" section to `docs/standards/MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md` pointing at `SprkModal`, `MODAL-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md`, and the size scale — so the decision doc and the implementation stay in lockstep; (2) add ONE pointer row to root `CLAUDE.md` §17 for `docs/standards/MODAL-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md`; (3) add a `.claude/CHANGELOG.md` entry (root §18 requires every root-CLAUDE.md PR to add one). This is FR-10 and MUST run in the main session. Documentation only — no code.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Spaarke documentation governance and the root CLAUDE.md pointer conventions. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>`docs/standards/MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md` gains a "Component Layer" section; root `CLAUDE.md` §17 gains one pointer row for `MODAL-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md`; `.claude/CHANGELOG.md` gains an entry covering the FR-10 standards/ADR/pattern doc set.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Design §5 + §7 / spec FR-10: the decision doc (`MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md`) and the new component layer must be linked both ways so a future author lands on the implementation from the decision, and root CLAUDE.md §17 (the pointer table the agent loads every session) must surface the new standard. Root CLAUDE.md §18 mandates a CHANGELOG entry for every PR touching root CLAUDE.md or `.claude/` — this task consolidates the CHANGELOG entry for the FR-10 doc/ADR/pattern set produced by tasks 010–012. Gated on 010 (the standard exists) and 011 (ADR-050 exists) so both are real targets to link.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">docs/standards/MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md</file>
      <file role="modify">CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file role="modify">.claude/CHANGELOG.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">docs/standards/MODAL-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md</file>
      <file role="reference">.claude/adr/ADR-050-canonical-modal-shell.md</file>
      <file role="reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/SprkModal/sizes.ts</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="010" status="pending">`MODAL-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md` — the standard both cross-links and the §17 row point at.</dependency>
      <dependency task="011" status="pending">ADR-050 — referenced from the component-layer section.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">The `MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md` edit is additive: add a "Component Layer" section that points at the `SprkModal` shell, `docs/standards/MODAL-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md`, ADR-050, and the size scale — do NOT alter the existing Two-Layout Standard, decision tree, or anti-patterns.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Add exactly ONE row to root `CLAUDE.md` §17 (Topic | Pointer) for `docs/standards/MODAL-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md`, placed beside its sibling `MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md` row. Do NOT restructure §17 or touch other rows.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Add a `.claude/CHANGELOG.md` entry under `[Unreleased]` in Keep-a-Changelog form (Added/Changed) that covers the FR-10 set: `MODAL-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md` (010), ADR-050 (011), `modal-shell.md` pointer (012), and this cross-link + §17 row. Root §18 requires it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Documentation only; NO code, NO BFF touch (NFR-05). Root CLAUDE.md is a hot-path file — make the minimal additive edit; do not reflow surrounding content.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>FR-10 documentation cross-linking</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-modal-system/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-modal-system/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md</file>
