    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Read `MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md`, root `CLAUDE.md` §17, and `.claude/CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]`. Confirm tasks 010/011 outputs exist. Run `/conflict-check` for in-flight root-CLAUDE.md §17 edits. Declare RIGOR: STANDARD.</step>
    <step order="1">Add a "Component Layer" section to `docs/standards/MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md` pointing at `SprkModal` + `MODAL-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md` + ADR-050 + the size scale (decision layer chooses the family; component layer implements the custom family).</step>
    <step order="2">Add ONE `MODAL-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md` pointer row to root `CLAUDE.md` §17, beside the `MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md` row.</step>
    <step order="3">Add the consolidated `.claude/CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]` entry (Added: `MODAL-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md`, ADR-050, `modal-shell.md`; Changed: `MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md` component-layer section + root §17 row).</step>
    <step order="4">Verify all cross-links resolve (relative paths), the §17 edit is a single additive row, and the CHANGELOG entry cites the FR-10 set.</step>
    <step order="5">Re-run `/conflict-check` before staging the root CLAUDE.md change; if a conflicting §17 edit merged in the meantime, reconcile at merge (do not clobber).</step>
    <step order="6">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set 013 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviation in `projects/spaarke-modal-system/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Root `CLAUDE.md` is a hot-path file shared with other active worktrees. If `/conflict-check` shows a conflicting §17 edit in flight (or one lands before merge), STOP and coordinate the merge per CLAUDE.md §6 rather than clobbering the other worktree's row — reconcile both additions at merge time.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
